ed read-aloud and seed picture set (Curio Class writes all four). Host: a wonder from the science unit running in the same weeks, for example sk-push-pull ("why did the ball stop?") in science grade K unit 1 (days 1 to 9); stand-alone: "What is inside a seed?" with the seed read-aloud and a real seed cut open by the teacher | The wonder and the cycle come first because every later unit opens with a question from the board and runs the four steps; the first weeks of school are when the class makes its board, and social studies kindergarten unit 1 starts its own wonder wall in the same weeks (one board serves both, see Cross-subject) | Candidate: the continuum's K wonder cell (making guesses about what a fiction or nonfiction book will be about from its cover) as a practice-day prompt before the read-aloud; the K connect cell (stating one or two new ideas learned from a read-aloud) at the share step | Neutral topic only (seeds; the rolling ball). No child is pushed to speak: a child may point at a picture or whisper the wonder to the teacher. The visiting staff member follows APPROACH.md "Sensitive ground" item 8: a neutral class topic, questions checked by the teacher first, and no question about home or family. The teacher cuts the seed; children only look. Whose voices: the unit records the makers of its read-aloud and pictures (C12) |
