res and the self-check, about ten minutes, then the regrouped reteach). Skill card: "look at the label, find the bin, bring it back" pictured. End-of-unit evidence (about 17 minutes for 30): at a station of five while the others do the story-or-fact sort in the book corner, each child brings back a book from a named bin not used in practice, says whether it is a story book or a fact book (k-picture-book-labels) and puts it back in the bin it lives in (k-library-visit), about 2.5 minutes a group, six groups; then, in the circle, each child holds a strip of the three stop pictures and, as the teacher describes an upsetting picture on a pretend screen, points at the steps in order (k-library-visit), scanned in about 2 minutes. Tools: bin label cards and stickers, the story-or-fact sort set, the stop rule picture cards and strips, the rain read-aloud (Curio Class writes the cards, the strips, the sort set and the read-aloud). Host: a fact book about weather for ela grade K unit 2 (days 35 to 76), or for sk-weather-watch in science grade K unit 2 (days 10 to 19); stand-alone: "What happens when rain falls?" | After unit 1 because the cycle's find step now becomes the child's own job: the class needs a question (unit 1) before it can fetch a book that might answer it; and before unit 3, which needs a fact book in hand | Candidate: the continuum's K cells that picture books can be true or not true, and that different tools in a library help find materials, folded into the sort and the bins; choosing a book of one's own interest on borrowing day (the continuum's PK to 2 personal-interest skill), kept as a borrowing-day choice, not a scored skill | Borrowing: many families have no library card and few books at home; borrowing is from the class book corner, no book goes home unless the school's own rules allow it, and no child is asked about books at home. Lost or damaged books are never a child's blame in front of the class. The stop rule: the teacher page says what the adult does if an upsetting picture ever appears on a screen (close it, the child tells, no blame) and points to health's steps if a child tells something worrying (APPROACH.md, Section field 1) |
