ate: the continuum's K cells on telling the main idea of a read-aloud and taking notes on facts by drawing or saying them, at the share step; its bold "identifies facts about a topic" is this unit's move | Animals eating other animals: the case set keeps to plant eaters (rabbits, a tortoise) so no read-aloud describes a hunt. Whose voices: the unit records the makers of its passages (C12) |
