ools: the tree read-aloud, three tree picture sets, the talking object (Curio Class writes the read-aloud and sets). Host: the trees research of ela grade K unit 3 (days 80 to 118) (ek-shared-research); stand-alone: "What lives in and around a tree?" | Last because it gathers the year: the question (unit 1), the fact book (unit 2) and the answering fact (unit 3) are what a child brings to the group; and the maker's name means most once children are sharing found facts that are not their own ideas | Candidate: the continuum's K cells on recognizing what feedback is and why it helps, and on listening and raising a hand before speaking, at the group turn; its bold on telling one's own ideas from others' ideas is taught here inside k-who-made-book | Honest use without shaming (APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground, item 4): a child who calls a found fact "mine" is helped to say "I found it in...", never corrected in front of the group. Groups are mixed by the teacher, never by background. A child who prefers not to speak may hand the talking object on and point at their fact. Whose voices: the unit records the makers of its read-aloud and pictures (C12) |

