ot new ownership. | The base text's module 3, its research module. Text features come with research because the bird texts are built to be searched. Syllables, open syllables and silent e come after short vowels and endings are secure, in the Skills Block's order; vowel teams and r-controlled vowels follow in unit 4 (r-controlled vowels are taught in grade 1). Unit 4 uses this unit's bird knowledge. | Candidate: the base text's module 3 unit assessments, adapted (main topic and key details; text features; the bird research piece; the riddle card) and the Skills Block checks for cycles 12 to 18 (syllables, open syllables, silent e; no vowel teams yet); checked in the unit plan. | Predators and prey named plainly, without graphic pictures. Outdoor bird watching: supervision; no touching nests, eggs or birds. Children with bird allergies or fears get a window or picture route. |
