UNIT 4 Sound. *Why does the rubber band go blurry when our box guitar plays, and why does the sound stop when we touch it?* Anchor: a shoebox guitar of stretched rubber bands DAYS 7 SKILLS s1-sound-vibrates

UNIT 5 Light. *Why can't we see the toy inside the box until we open the flap, and why does a beam show a bright patch behind wax paper but a shadow behind cardboard?* Anchor: a shoebox with a peephole and a toy inside, flap shut then open DAYS 10 SKILLS s1-see-with-light; s1-light-materials

UNIT 6 Sending a message. *How can we tell a friend across the playground it is time to come in, without shouting?* Design problem: a message that must cross the playground or a long hallway Anchor: one ring of the school bell or one whistle at the end of recess calls the whole playground in at once, with no one shouting; design problem: build a light or sound signal that tells a friend across the playground or a long hallway it is time to come in DAYS 8 SKILLS s1-signal-device

UNIT 7 Parents and young. *Why does a baby bird cheep with its mouth open when its parent lands on the nest?* Anchor: a public-domain video of an American robin nest at feeding time DAYS 6 SKILLS s1-parent-offspring

UNIT 8 Daylight and the seasons. *Is it light or dark at 5:30 in the evening, and will spring be like fall or like winter?* Anchor: the class's own daylight chart, started on day 9, just after unit 1, and marked each month from optional family reports, beside its monthly day strips DAYS 5 SKILLS s1-daylight-seasons

