{'strand': 'reading-informational', 'grade': '1', 'skill_id': 'e1-main-topic', 'standard': 'RI.1.2', 'assumes': 'ek-main-topic', 'hands_on': 'e2-main-topic-paragraphs', 'model_in': 'main-idea-details', 'model_out': 'main-idea-details', 'words': 'main topic; key detail; retell; about', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Identify the main topic and retell key details of an informational text (RI.1.2). Practised on informational read-alouds and short texts on tools and work, the sun, moon and stars, and birds' bodies, using main-idea-details. Grows from kindergarten by dropping 'with prompting and support' (ek-main-topic). Boundary: one topic per text; grade 2 adds multiparagraph text and the focus of each paragraph (RI.2.2)."}
{'strand': 'reading-informational', 'grade': '1', 'skill_id': 'e1-text-features', 'standard': 'RI.1.5', 'assumes': 'ek-books-and-authors', 'hands_on': 'e2-text-features', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'heading; table of contents; glossary; label; caption; icon; menu', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Know and use text features (headings, table of contents, glossary, labels, electronic menus and icons) to find key facts (RI.1.5). Practised on informational books about birds (module 3, the research module) and on a simple Curio Class web page. Grows from kindergarten's cover, back cover and title page (ek-books-and-authors). Boundary: grade 2 adds captions, bold print, subheadings and index and asks for efficient use (RI.2.5)."}
{'strand': 'writing', 'grade': '1', 'skill_id': 'e1-informative', 'standard': 'W.1.2', 'assumes': 'ek-inform', 'hands_on': 'e2-informative', 'model_in': 'main-idea-details', 'model_out': 'main-idea-details; paragraph-frame', 'words': 'topic; fact; teach; closing; paragraph', 'cross_subject': 'science:1-LS1-1 (how birds use body parts to survive)', 'notes': "Write an informative piece that names a topic, gives some facts about it and gives some sense of closure (W.1.2): how a tool helps do a job (module 1), how beaks or feathers help birds survive (module 3, an informational paragraph from research). Introduces paragraph-frame (an opening sentence, a middle with the facts, a closing sentence, color-coded) and uses main-idea-details. Grows from kindergarten's naming and some information (ek-inform) by asking for facts and an ending. Boundary: several facts on one topic; definitions and a concluding section are grade 2 (W.2.2)."}
{'strand': 'writing', 'grade': '1', 'skill_id': 'e1-shared-research', 'standard': 'W.1.7; W.1.8', 'assumes': 'ek-shared-research', 'hands_on': 'e2-research', 'model_in': 'research-cycle', 'model_out': 'research-cycle', 'words': 'research; question; notes; source; expert; observe', 'cross_subject': 'science:1-LS1-1 (shared research on bird body parts)', 'notes': "Take part in shared research and writing projects, such as reading several how-to books and writing instructions (W.1.7), and, with help, recall information from experience or gather it from provided sources to answer a question (W.1.8). Practised in the sky notebook (module 2) and the whole-class then small-group research on birds' beaks and feathers (module 3). Grows from kindergarten's same wording by asking for notes in words and a product written from more than one source. Boundary: sources are provided; grade 2 removes 'with guidance and support' from W.2.8."}
{'strand': 'speaking-listening', 'grade': '1', 'skill_id': 'e1-discussion', 'standard': 'SL.1.1; SL.1.3', 'assumes': 'ek-discussion', 'hands_on': 'e2-discussion', 'model_in': 'discussion-protocol', 'model_out': 'discussion-protocol', 'words': 'listen with care; one at a time; build on; I agree; I want to add; clarify', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Collaborative conversations about grade 1 topics and texts: follow agreed rules, listening with care and speaking one at a time (SL.1.1a), build on others' talk through several exchanges (SL.1.1b), and ask questions to clear up confusion (SL.1.1c); ask and answer questions about what a speaker says to gather information or clarify (SL.1.3). Practised in science talks about sky patterns (module 2) and small-group talk about illustrations (module 3). Grows from kindergarten's continuing a conversation (ek-discussion) to building on another's comment. Boundary: frames fade across the year; grade 2 links comments to others' remarks (SL.2.1b). A named protocol on the module text most days, at least two a week, as the base text runs them."}
