# note: edition confirmed at source 2026-11-16: standards.aasl.org presents the "Second Edition" and links the learner framework PDF named 250918 (2025-09-18); still six Shared Foundations. Reuse terms (standards.aasl.org/permissions, read 2026-11-16): a single competency may be excerpted into a lesson or unit plan for non-commercial education; the whole framework or a substantial part needs ALA permission. So this file and Curio Class pages hold ids and our own words only.
# level: one learner competency, AASL.<Shared Foundation>.<Domain>.<n>, e.g. AASL.I.A.1
# note: Shared Foundations: I Inquire, II Include, III Collaborate, IV Curate, V Explore, VI Engage. Domains: A Think, B Create, C Share, D Grow. modules.csv codes AASL.Inquire etc., so map the name to its numeral before prefix-matching (AASL.Inquire -> AASL.I.).
