## Seams

### Picked up from the course before

Kindergarten has no course before it in Curio Class. The rows' assumes are empty: the course assumes no library
skill, only children who can listen to a short read-aloud and take a turn in a circle with help, which unit 1 and
unit 4 teach anyway. No unit opens with a readiness check.

### Handed on to Library and Research Skills, grade 1

| This course hands on | Unit here | Grade 1 row that picks it up | What grade 1 does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| k-wonder: an "I wonder" question of one's own, the class wonder board | 1 | g1-what-i-know | A know and wonder sheet before a read-aloud; owns AASL.I.A.2 |
| k-class-inquiry: the whole cycle once a unit as four pictures (research-cycle) | 1 | g1-class-book; g1-star-and-wish | A class information book, one page per child; a star and a wish on a classmate's page |
| k-library-visit: caring for books, putting a book back, borrowing day, the stop rule as pictured words | 2 | g1-device-stop-rule | The stop rule practiced on a shared class device, and never typing a name or school |
| k-picture-book-labels: a book fetched from a named bin, story books and fact books sorted | 2 | g1-story-or-fact-book | Choosing the information book for a question and saying why |
| k-listen-and-retell: listening for the part that answers one held question | 3 | g1-find-in-a-book | Using cover, contents, headings and pictures to find the answering page |
| k-talk-in-group: turns in a group of three, saying what each friend added | 4 | g1-group-helpers | Pictured group jobs (finder, holder, teller), swapped each time |
| k-who-made-book: a person made this book, the author and illustrator named | 4 | g1-author-and-title | "I found this in the book (title) by (author)," copied onto a sticky note with help |

Every kindergarten row hands on to a grade 1 row, and each grade 1 row's assumes names it back.

